###
#  summary: 'GraphQL endpoint: cart, orders and products (15 operations)'
#  description: |-
#    All GraphQL operations go through this one URL. Send a JSON body with a query string. Pick an operation from the Examples dropdown.
#
#    Every call needs a bearer token. Role checks run per operation: a signed-in user with the wrong role gets a FORBIDDEN error inside the response.
#
#    **Queries (5)**
#    - me: any signed-in user. Returns publicId and role.
#    - myCart: client. The cart with its lines and total. Unavailable products stay in the list with available false and are left out of the total.
#    - myOrders(page = 1, size = 20): client. My orders, newest first. size above 100 is reduced to 100.
#    - order(id): client. One of my orders. A missing id, an invalid id and another client's order all return NOT_FOUND.
#    - orders(page = 1, size = 20, status, createdFrom, createdTo, clientEmail): manager. All orders, newest first. Optional filters, combined: status (PENDING, CONFIRMED, SHIPPED, DELIVERED or CANCELLED), createdFrom and createdTo (YYYY-MM-DD, both days included, UTC) and clientEmail (exact, case ignored; an unknown email gives an empty page). Bad values give VALIDATION_ERROR with every wrong field. Each order has a client field (id, email, firstName, lastName), manager only: a client who asks for it on myOrders, order or checkout gets FORBIDDEN on that field.
#
#    **Mutations (10)**
#    - addToCart(productId, quantity): client. Quantity must be above 0. The cart total for a product cannot exceed its stock.
#    - updateCartItemQuantity(productId, quantity): client. A quantity of 0 removes the line.
#    - removeFromCart(productId): client.
#    - checkout: client. Needs a non-empty cart. Creates the order, takes the stock, confirms the order and empties the cart in one transaction. If any product is unavailable or short on stock the whole checkout is refused with CONFLICT.
#    - shipOrder(id, trackingNumber, estimatedDelivery): manager. estimatedDelivery is a date, YYYY-MM-DD. trackingNumber has at most 64 characters.
#    - deliverOrder(id): manager.
#    - cancelOrder(id): manager. The stock goes back to the products.
#    - disableProduct(id): manager. Hides the product from the public reads and from new carts.
#    - enableProduct(id): manager. Shows the product again.
